{"id":"overview-working-with-objects-field-selectors","corpus":"k8s","title":"Field Selectors","sourceUrl":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/working-with-objects/field-selectors/","license":"Kubernetes Documentation © The Kubernetes Authors, licensed CC BY 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","blocks":[{"kind":"h1","text":"Field Selectors"},{"kind":"p","text":"Field selectors let you select Kubernetes objects based on the value of one or more resource fields. Here are some examples of field selector queries:"},{"kind":"li","text":"metadata.name=my-service"},{"kind":"li","text":"metadata.namespace!=default"},{"kind":"li","text":"status.phase=Pending"},{"kind":"p","text":"This kubectl command selects all Pods for which the value of the status.phase field is Running:"},{"kind":"p","text":"Field selectors are essentially resource filters. By default, no selectors/filters are applied, meaning that all resources of the specified type are selected. This makes the kubectl queries kubectl get pods and kubectl get pods --field-selector \"\" equivalent."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Supported fields"},{"kind":"p","text":"Supported field selectors vary by Kubernetes resource type. All resource types support the metadata.name and metadata.namespace fields. Using unsupported field selectors produces an error. For example:"},{"kind":"h3","text":"Custom resources fields"},{"kind":"p","text":"All custom resource types support the metadata.name and metadata.namespace fields."},{"kind":"p","text":"Additionally, the spec.versions[*].selectableFields field of a CustomResourceDefinition declares which other fields in a custom resource may be used in field selectors. See selectable fields for custom resources for more information about how to use field selectors with CustomResourceDefinitions."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Supported operators"},{"kind":"p","text":"You can use the =, ==, and != operators with field selectors (= and == mean the same thing). This kubectl command, for example, selects all Kubernetes Services that aren't in the default namespace:"},{"kind":"p","text":"Set-based operators (in, notin, exists) are not supported for field selectors."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Chained selectors"},{"kind":"p","text":"As with label and other selectors, field selectors can be chained together as a comma-separated list. This kubectl command selects all Pods for which the status.phase does not equal Running and the spec.restartPolicy field equals Always:"},{"kind":"h2","text":"Multiple resource types"},{"kind":"p","text":"You can use field selectors across multiple resource types. This kubectl command selects all Statefulsets and Services that are not in the default namespace:"}],"lemmas":{"fielded":["fielded","field"],"fielding":["fielding","field"],"selectors":["selector","selectors"],"lets":["let","lets"],"letting":["letting","let"],"selecting":["selecting","select"],"kubernetes":["kubernetes","kubernete"],"objects":["object","objects"],"objected":["objected","object"],"objecting":["objecting","object"],"based":["based","base"],"baseds":["baseds","based"],"bases":["base","bases"],"basing":["basing","base"],"values":["value","values"],"valuing":["valuing","value"],"valued":["valued","value"],"ones":["one","ones"],"fields":["field","fields"],"examples":["example","examples"],"queries":["query","queries"],"metadata":["metadata","metadatum"],"names":["name","names"],"naming":["naming","name"],"named":["named","name"],"serviced":["serviced","service"],"servicing":["servicing","service"],"namespaces":["namespaces","namespace"],"defaults":["default","defaults"],"statuses":["status","statuses"],"phases":["phase","phases"],"phasing":["phasing","phase"],"phased":["phased","phase"],"pendings":["pendings","pending"],"kubectls":["kubectls","kubectl"],"commands":["command","commands"],"commanded":["commanded","command"],"commanding":["commanding","command"],"selects":["selects","select"],"pods":["pod","pods"],"running":["running","run"]